Preferred: int[] numbers;  — brackets after type (Java style)
Also valid: int numbers[];  — brackets after name (C-style, avoid)
For objects: String[] names;
For 2D: int[][] matrix;
Declaration alone allocates NO memory — the variable is null until assigned.

int[] primes = {2, 3, 5, 7, 11};  — size inferred from values
String[] days = {"Mon", "Tue", "Wed", "Thu", "Fri"};
This syntax is ONLY valid at the point of declaration.
Cannot use: numbers = {1,2,3}; — must be: numbers = new int[]{1,2,3};

