int[] arr = {34, 7, 89, 12, 56, 3};
int max = arr[0]; // Start with first element, not 0
for (int i = 1; i < arr.length; i++) {
    if (arr[i] > max) {
        max = arr[i];
    }
}
System.out.println("Max: " + max); // Output: 89
Key point: Initialize max with arr[0] (not 0 or Integer.MIN_VALUE) for correctness with negative arrays. Start loop at i = 1 since we already checked index 0.

