int[] arr = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
int left = 0, right = arr.length - 1;
while (left < right) {
    int temp = arr[left];
    arr[left] = arr[right];
    arr[right] = temp;
    left++;
    right--;
}
System.out.println(Arrays.toString(arr)); // Output: [5, 4, 3, 2, 1]
Algorithm: Two-pointer swap from both ends moving inward. Works for both even and odd length arrays. O(n/2) swaps = O(n) time, O(1) space — no new array created.

